on.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c14"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c14"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c14","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.82 (An equivalent vanishing condition)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.82, p. 68, label record:257bm-c14","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n \\forall\\ \\text{skipped rank }n\\ge3\\text{ whose actual word equals the seam-greedy word},\\\\\n \\text{the integer remainder at }n\\text{ is zero}.\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\nThis condition is equivalent to Definition 6.81. At an actual skipped rank, the source proves that $F(n-1,n)<0$ holds exactly when the real prefix agrees with the integer greedy word and its integer remainder is positive. On agreement, $F(n-1,n)$ is the negative of that nonnegative remainder. Thus nonnegativity of the margin at every skip is equivalent to vanishing of the remainder at every aligned skip. The equivalence is proved; neither condition is established for all required ranks.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-c14","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-c14","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c14%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.greedyHalfFrozenMargin_fullShell_eq_neg_seamRemainder_of_alignment%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c14%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.greedyHalfFrozenMargin_fullShell_eq_neg_seamRemainder_of_alignment%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.greedyHalfFrozenMargin_fullShell_eq_neg_seamRemainder_